/-!
# `A = (ω,ω,1 | ω,ω,1 | 2,0,0)` is a P-position

GENERATED by `scripts/lean_A_gen.py`. Do not edit.

The positions with infinite columns in the proof: 46 positions with two infinite columns
(7 of them P, among them the two rods `2 × ω`), the options of `A`, and `A`.
A position with two infinite columns is shown to be P by going through its bites: a cut of the
poison column leaves a finite position with a reply into `S` (lemmas `fc_…`); a cut of the other
infinite column leaves one infinite column (`fundamental`); a bite in a finite column leaves one
of the positions treated before. A position is shown to be N by one bite.
-/

